course: dictionary
lesson: 6899
title: Ovules inside the flower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flower has many parts, and some are hidden inside. An ovule is one of these tiny hidden parts. It sits inside the ovary, the swollen bottom part of the flower's female part. «A flower has petals, stamens that make pollen and a carpel in the middle holding tiny ovules.» So the ovules are kept safe inside the flower.
explain: An ovule is not a seed yet. It waits for pollen to arrive. When pollen joins it, this is called fertilisation. «After pollination, the pollen and the ovule join (fertilisation), the ovule becomes a seed.» So the ovule is where a new seed begins.
explain: Use the clue words around ovule. Ovary, pollen, fertilisation and seed all sit near it in the sentences, and they show you what an ovule does. Ask yourself: what happens to the ovule next? The answer is that it becomes a seed. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: An ovule is a tiny part inside the ovary of a flower.
fact: The ovary is the swollen bottom part of the pistil, the female part of a flower.
fact: Pollen must reach the ovule before fertilisation can happen.
fact: When an ovule is fertilised, it becomes a seed.
fact: «In its middle are the stamens, which make a fine powder called pollen, and the pistil, which holds tiny eggs called ovules.» This sentence compares ovules to tiny eggs, because both wait to be joined by another cell.
exercise: «A flower has petals, stamens that make pollen and a carpel in the middle holding tiny ovules.» Where are the ovules kept? | In the roots | On the stamens | *Inside the ovary | In the petals
exercise: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds.» What does an ovule become after fertilisation? | A petal | A stem | *A seed | Pollen
exercise: «After pollination, the pollen and the ovule join (fertilisation).» Find and copy the word for the fine powder that joins with the ovule. | stigma | *pollen | ovary | petal
test: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the flower's ovary grows into a fruit.» What does the ovary grow into? | A root | A petal | A leaf | *A fruit
test: What is an ovule? | *A tiny part inside the ovary that becomes a seed after fertilisation | A bright coloured petal | A stem that holds up the flower | The powder that sticks to bees
exam: What happens first, after pollination? | The ovule becomes a seed | The ovary grows into a fruit | *Pollen reaches the ovule | The petals fall off
